%N A400300 Composite numbers that are equal to the concatenation of the primes and exponents in their canonical prime factorizations in some bijective base.
%C A400300 A368107 is a subsequence. For every prime p and positive integer m divisible by p, let b = (p^m - m)/p. If p^m > 4, then b >= m >= p, and hence the concatenation of p and m in bijective base b represents p*b + m = p^m. The exceptional term 4 is obtained in bijective base 1 by concatenating 11 and 11.
%C A400300 This sequence has substantial overlap with A384537. The smallest term of A384537 that is not in this sequence is 255987 = 3^3 * 19 * 499, which satisfies the defining condition of A384537 in ordinary base 2, but not in any bijective base.
%C A400300 Unlike A384537, which contains no squarefree numbers, this sequence contains squarefree terms, such as 1155 = 3*5*7*11 and 17931 = 3*43*139.
%C A400300 The terms a(37) through a(41) are 268435456, 290462031, 387420489, and 1073741824, 3301896361 all of which also belong to A384537. The two nontrivial term among them is a(38) = 290462031 = 3^10 * 4919 = (3,10,4919) in base 9838 and a(41) = 290462031 = 144D299E1(15) = 14 * 4D^2 * 99E1 (in decimal: 3301896361 = 19 * 73^2 * 32611) in base 15.
%H A400300 Donghwi Park, <a href="https://github.com/gwahak/mathematics/blob/master/A400300.ipynb">Python program</a>.
%H A400300 Donghwi Park, <a href="https://github.com/gwahak/mathematics/blob/master/A400300_u32.c">C program for searching additional terms, up to 2^32-1</a>.
%H A400300 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bijective_numeration">Bijective numeration</a>.
